---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
const path = '/privacy/';
---
<Base title="Elora Privacy — Local Data & Optional Cloud Connections" description="Understand what stays on your PC, what optional Groq and Google connections send, and how Elora handles voice, screen context and action approvals." pageType="AboutPage" breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy', path }]}>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Clear boundaries" title="Local first. Clear about what leaves." lead="Elora stores her memory on your PC. Connected features change where some audio and text are processed. Here is how those choices work." crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy', path }]} />
  <div class="bg-surface px-4 pb-24 sm:px-6">
    <article class="prose-elora mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h2 id="on-your-pc">What stays on your PC</h2>
      <p>The background brain, vision, embeddings and memory storage run locally. Conversations, observations and facts are stored in local SQLite and vector data files. Local chat uses Ollama; local speech recognition and local voices are available without cloud processing after their models are installed.</p>
      <p><strong>Local storage and local processing are different.</strong> Keeping memory on disk does not mean that retrieved context cannot appear in an optional cloud chat request.</p>
      <h2 id="internet">What optional connections send</h2>
      <div class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[540px] text-left text-body-sm">
          <caption class="sr-only">Data sent by optional connected features</caption>
          <thead class="bg-surface-container-high text-primary"><tr><th scope="col" class="p-4">Feature</th><th scope="col" class="p-4">What can leave</th><th scope="col" class="p-4">Destination</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody class="text-on-surface-variant">
            <tr class="border-t border-white/10"><th scope="row" class="p-4 font-medium">Cloud speech</th><td class="p-4">Captured speech or enabled meeting-audio chunks</td><td class="p-4">GroqCloud</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-white/10"><th scope="row" class="p-4 font-medium">Cloud chat</th><td class="p-4">Messages and context included in the prompt</td><td class="p-4">GroqCloud</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-white/10"><th scope="row" class="p-4 font-medium">Cloud voice</th><td class="p-4">Text to be spoken aloud</td><td class="p-4">GroqCloud</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-white/10"><th scope="row" class="p-4 font-medium">Desktop agent</th><td class="p-4">Redacted focused-window text and task context; no screenshots</td><td class="p-4">GroqCloud</td></tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-white/10"><th scope="row" class="p-4 font-medium">Google Workspace</th><td class="p-4">Authorized account queries and approved writes</td><td class="p-4">Google; content may also enter enabled cloud chat or voice</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Groq speech, chat and voice are separate opt-ins and require hybrid network mode. Cloud failures fall back to the configured local engines. Keys and card/ID-like numbers are masked before applicable cloud requests; this does not remove every kind of personal information.</p>
      <p>Google access requires your own OAuth setup and sign-in. To process Google content with local chat and voice, disable Groq chat and Groq TTS; Google itself remains an online service. You can disable the Workspace server or revoke its account access.</p>
      <p>Optional online research and other explicitly enabled network tools contact the services they use. Initial model and dependency downloads also need internet access. Provider processing and retention depend on the provider and your account settings.</p>
      <h2 id="screen">Screen context and desktop actions</h2>
      <p>When enabled, screen perception reads text and window context locally. OCR, email and tool results are treated as untrusted input rather than standing instructions. These protections reduce risk; they are not a promise that every possible prompt injection is detectable.</p>
      <p>The desktop agent only runs on your request. Clicks, typing and launching applications are owner-directed actions. PowerShell, closing programs, registry and raw file operations wait for approval in the HUD. The autonomous brain cannot use this agent.</p>
      <h2 id="voice">Microphone choices</h2>
      <p>Push-to-talk captures speech while you hold the HUD mic button. A warm microphone can retain a short, 0.3-second in-memory buffer between presses; it can be disabled. Optional hands-free mode keeps the mic open for a local name check. Meeting and system-audio capture are separate optional features.</p>
      <p>Transcription is local by default. With Groq speech enabled, captured clips go to GroqCloud. Experimental full-duplex browser call mode is a separate voice experience.</p>
      <h2 id="control">Your controls</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Privacy mode</strong> pauses perception; the stealth control hides the UI.</li>
        <li><strong>Google writes</strong> such as drafts, sends, uploads and calendar changes require approval; deletes are classified as irreversible.</li>
        <li><strong>Local data</strong> can be inspected and maintained with the product's reset tools. Check their scope: logs, models and credentials may need separate handling.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloud copies</strong> are not removed by deleting local data. Manage connected accounts separately.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
      <p>This site's code sets no cookies and includes no analytics or tracking scripts. Fonts and illustration assets are served from this site. The hosting provider may keep standard access logs, including IP addresses. This website currently has no active email signup form.</p>
      <p>Production pages use the canonical address <a href="https://eloraos.com/">https://eloraos.com/</a>.</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-tele-sm text-outline">Product information reviewed <time datetime={SITE.contentUpdated}>{SITE.contentUpdatedLabel}</time>.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <CtaBand />
</Base>
